# Architecture

Go API + React `frontend/`, PostgreSQL. Extend the existing modules. Words: `GLOSSARY.md`. Why: `docs/adr/`. Shape: `docs/architecture/`.

HTTP adapters bind, call an interface in `internal/services`, and map errors. Logic in `backend/internal/logic/**` implements those interfaces. SQL lives in `backend/internal/repositories`. `internal/app/server.go` wires repositories into logic and passes the logic to the adapters. Before coding, read that path and `docs/architecture/directory-structure.md`.

## Invariants

| Concern | Rule |
|---------|------|
| Stock state | In stock when `stocked_out_on` is null. No stock-state column (ADR-0005) |
| Inventory age | Calendar days from `entered_on`; stops on `stocked_out_on` when set |
| Aging stock | In stock and inventory age > 90. The API owns this rule |
| Stocked out | Row stays (ADR-0001). No return to in stock. VIN is never reused (ADR-0004) |
| Identity | Vehicle address is an app-minted snowflake bigint (JSON string on the wire). Make and model addresses are identity integers. VIN is the business identity, unique via `vehicle_vins`, and immutable after record (ADR-0006, ADR-0011, ADR-0012, ADR-0013) |
| Catalog | Vehicle stores `model_id` (ADR-0002) |
| Commands | Stock-out and proposed action are separate routes (ADR-0007) |
| Proposed action | Optional: price reduction planned, wholesale planned, or hold. A new value replaces the last |
| Origin | `/api/v1` and the UI on one origin (ADR-0009) |

Use glossary terms in code, API, UI, and docs. A behavior change updates the owning doc in the same change. An invariant change needs a new ADR. Tests cover aging boundaries, terminal stocked-out, VIN uniqueness, and command isolation.
